## 3. Shape First & Exact Constants: `IRR` (`dc-j9k.102`–`105` — `22,749 / 22,749`, checked)

1. **Leading-Zero Cashflow Strip (`dc-j9k.102`, checked)**: Advance past leading `flow == 0.0` (`let start = cashflows.iter().position(|&x| x != 0.0)`) before discounting; if all flows are `0.0` (`None`), return `#NUM!`. Factoring out `base^-start` makes leading zeros exact no-ops while keeping interior and trailing zeros active (`power = mul(power, base)` still advances on trailing `0.0`s and triggers `#DIV/0!` on `power` underflow/overflow).
2. **No Sign-Change Pre-Check in `irr_kernel` (`dc-j9k.104`, checked)**: Check only finiteness (`!flow.is_finite() -> #VALUE!`) and non-empty after leading-zero strip (`len < 1 -> #NUM!`), letting single-sign arrays enter `irr_u_secant` (where `power` underflow returns `#DIV/0!` instead of `#NUM!`, fixing `800+` single-sign rows and `I-C` `16/16`). Keep `validate_cashflows` unchanged for `XIRR`/`MIRR`.
3. **Symmetric Pole Gate `v = sub(1.0, u) >= 1e-7` In-Loop & `>= 1e-4` Post-Budget (`dc-j9k.104`, checked)**: Mirroring `RATE`'s `add(1.0, r) >= 1e-7` (in-loop) and `>= 1e-4` (`iter == 200`), `IRR` rejects `v < 1e-7` in-loop (`1 + r > 1e7`) and `v < 1e-4` post-budget (`1 + r > 1e4`) as `RetryNum`, so early guesses retry `0.1`, `-0.1`, `2/3` and find moderate roots (`I3-huge-vs-moderate-root`, `14 / 14` `sf2` bisected frontiers to `0 ULP`, `I-B` `20/20`).
4. **3-Way Typed Status (`RetryNum`, `HardNum`, `HardDiv0`) & Post-Loop `!total.is_finite()` (`dc-j9k.103`, `dc-j9k.105`, checked)**:
   - Replacing `Option<f64>` with `IrrStep { Ok(f64), RetryNum, HardNum, HardDiv0 }` stops `#DIV/0!` and overflow `#NUM!` from being swallowed by the guess-retry ladder.
   - In `npv(u)`: `v == 0.0`, `!base.is_finite() || base == 0.0`, and `!divisor.is_finite() || divisor == 0.0` (`divisor = irr_daz(power)`) return `HardDiv0`. Accumulate `total = add(total, irr_daz(div(flow, divisor)))` across all `k` **without** per-term finiteness exit, then check `if !total.is_finite() { return HardNum; }` after the loop (`I-E` `16/16`).
   - In secant loop: `irr_daz(change) == 0.0 -> HardDiv0`; `!next.is_finite() -> HardNum`; double-flat, failed `publish`, or 200-step exhaustion -> `RetryNum`.
5. **Unified 16-Bit High-Word `rgw[3] == 0` (`[0.0, +2^-1026)`) Flat Check & Strict `>` (`checked`)**: On little-endian x86 IEEE-754 `double` (`USHORT rgw[4]`), `rgw[3] == 0` (`(bits >> 48) == 0`) tests `0.0 <= dy < 2^-1026` (`f64::MIN_POSITIVE / 16.0`). `RATE` formed `dy = y0 - y1` (`-2^-1026 < change <= 0.0`); `IRR` formed `dy = y1 - y0` (`0.0 <= change < f64::MIN_POSITIVE / 16.0`), nudging `before` by `if current > before { 0.001 } else { -0.001 }` and returning `RetryNum` on second flat (`I-A` `20/20`, `I-F` `12/12`, resolving the final `15` `sf2` `IRR` rows to `22,749 / 22,749`).

